  q\protect \,L_c\approx 251$ and different bins write mutually orthogonal
  gratings. In our one-dimensional space--time simulation of a two-bin,
  mode-selective write, the selectivity between the targeted and the orthogonal
  bin superposition drops to 0.5, i.e.\ no selectivity. The scheme would also
  need meter-scale interaction lengths ($\approx $1.3~m for 100-MHz photons)
